The Vitoria-Gasteiz Local Police’s Accident Reports Section has launched an investigation into a 47-year-old man suspected of committing a road safety violation. The case stems from his alleged driving under the influence of alcohol and other substances following an incident yesterday afternoon. The crash occurred shortly after 4:00 p.m. on Donostia Street, where the driver struck two parked vehicles and a traffic sign.

Forensic tests confirmed a severe impairment: the man’s breathalyzer results registered 1.17 and 1.19 milligrams of alcohol per liter of exhaled air—four times the legal limit. Additionally, his tests came back positive for cocaine, significantly worsening his criminal liability.

This incident follows a string of road accidents in Álava’s capital over the past hours. Authorities have recorded a total of 16 additional crashes, leaving two people injured. The most recent incident occurred early this morning at 5:30 a.m., when a 29-year-old cyclist collided with an electric scooter. The woman suffered injuries requiring immediate transport to a hospital for treatment.

Separately, a 55-year-old woman was injured yesterday in a car collision, one of the vehicles involved being hers.

Beyond traffic-related incidents, the judicial police have been highly active, filing 24 complaints. These include:
- One for discovery and disclosure of secrets;
- Ten for theft, including three bicycle thefts, two involving personal micromobility vehicles (PMVs), and one involving items stolen from inside a vehicle;
- One for robbery with violence;
- Two for robbery with force, one of which also occurred inside a vehicle;
- Three for fraud;
- Three for property damage; and
- Four for losses.
